I would say that the net effect of gaining levels can be negative if you
don't exploit the benefits to the maximum - for example, those extra skill
slots do you no good if you don't use them to improve performance with
weapons you use, but if you can and do use them to improve thrown dagger
performance the effect can be devastating. Conversely it is very easy to
exploit the benefit of weaker monster generation - the game does it for
you by generating weaker monsters.

This is why we see the protection racket is popular initially but is not
picked by the very best players.
